=== HINT 1 ===
constexpr syntax (C23):
  constexpr int NAME = value;
  constexpr double NAME = value;

It must be initialized with a constant expression.

=== HINT 2 ===
Remove the #define lines and replace with:
  constexpr int    BUFFER_SIZE = 64;
  constexpr int    MAX_RETRIES = 3;
  constexpr double GRAVITY     = 9.81;

=== HINT 3 ===
constexpr integrates with the type system - you get proper type checking,
unlike #define which is a raw text substitution.

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
constexpr int    BUFFER_SIZE = 64;
constexpr int    MAX_RETRIES = 3;
constexpr double GRAVITY     = 9.81;
